## Project Overview

Mizizi (Swahili for "roots") is a daily 20-minute language and cultural 
preservation app for diaspora and international students. It helps users 
maintain their heritage language through creative expression, not grammar 
drills. It also learns the user's culture *from the user* — refining its 
understanding through feedback until the user feels genuinely represented.

The core design principle: AI is the student. The user is the authority 
on their own culture.

